__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
.venv/
venv/
ENV/
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
.DS_Store

# Local market data only. A bare "data/" would also swallow the source packages
# src/trading_system/data/ and tests/data/, so both patterns are anchored.
/data/
*.parquet

.env
*.log
.claude/

# Stored runs. Anchored for the same reason /data/ is: a bare "runs/" would also
# match any package directory of that name.
/runs/

# Generated HTML reports: a few megabytes of plotly per page, rebuilt from
# runs/ on demand by `ts report`. Anchored for the same reason /runs/ is.
/reports/

# Converted scraped specs, staged for inspection before import. Regenerated by
# `ts strategy ingest convert`; the copy that matters is the one in
# strategies/library/, which is under version control.
/strategies/ingest_converted/

# The scrape itself: raw input to `ts strategy ingest`, dropped in by hand and
# replaceable at any time. These are pages about strategies, not strategies —
# prose and screenshots someone else wrote, none of it validated, most of it
# not even expressible as a spec (883 cards in, 1 out; see the P00 section of
# CLAUDE.md). Untracked so that nothing here can be mistaken for a candidate:
# a card becomes one only by converting into strategies/library/ and being
# measured there. Not in git also because it is a third party's corpus, sizeable
# and regenerable, with no bearing on what the code does.
/strategies/scraped_strategies_v3/
